{
  "title": "Namaz of Imam al-Kazim (a.s.)",
  "data": "Upon concluding the prayer, say the following supplication:\nاِلٰهِيْ خَشَعَتِ الْاَصْوَاتُ لَكَ\nILAAHEE KHASHA'ATIL ASWAATU LAK\nO my God, all sounds are submissive to You,\nوَضَلَّتِ الْاَحْلَامُ فِيْكَ\nWA DALLATIL AHLAAMU FEEK\nall intellects are too short to recognize You [as exactly as You are],\nوَوَجِلَ كُلُّ شَيْءٍ مِنْكَ\nWA WAJILA KULLU SHAY'IN MINK\nall things are fearful of You,\nوَهَرَبَ كُلُّ شَيْءٍ اِلَيْكَ\nWA HARABA KULLU SHAY'IN ILAYK\nall things flee to You,\nوَضَاقَتِ الْاَشْيَاءُ دُوْنَكَ\nWA DAAQATIL ASHYAA'U DOONAK\nall things are too tiny in comparison with You,\nوَمَلَاَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ نُوْرُكَ\nWA MALA'A KULLA SHAY'IN NOORUK\nand Your light fills all things.\nفَاَنْتَ الرَّفِيْعُ فِيْ جَلَالِكَ\nFA-ANTAR RAFEE'U FEE JALAALIK\nTherefore, You are the Exalted in Your majesty,\nوَاَنْتَ الْبَهِيُّ فِيْ جَمَالِكَ\nWA ANTAL BAHIYYU FEE JAMAALIK\nYou are the Luminous in Your splendor,\nوَاَنْتَ الْعَظِيْمُ فِيْ قُدْرَتِكَ\nWA ANTAL A'ZEEMU FEE QUDRATIK\nYou are the Great in Your omnipotence,\nوَاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ لَا يَؤُوْدُكَ شَيْءٌ\nWA ANTAL LADHEE LAA YA'OODUKA SHAY'\nand You are Whom nothing can tire.\nيَا مُنْزِلَ نِعْمَتِيْ\nYAA MUNZILA NI'MATEE\nO He Who sends down my bounties!\nيَا مُفَرِّجَ كُرْبَتِيْ\nYAA MUFARRIJA KURBATEE\nO He Who relieves my agonies!\nوَيَا قَاضِيَ حَاجَتِيْ\nWA YAA QAADIYA HAAJATEE\nO He Who settles my needs!\nاَعْطِنِيْ مَسْاَلَتِيْ\nA'TINEE MAS'ALATEE\n(please) Give answer to my request,\nبِلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nBILAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nin the name of \"There is no god save You.\"\nآمَنْتُ بِكَ مُخْلِصاً لَكَ دِيْنِيْ\nAAMANTU BIKA MUKHLISAN LAKA DEENEE\nI believe in You and I am sincere to You in obedience.\nاَصْبَحْتُ عَلٰى عَهْدِكَ وَوَعْدِكَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُ\nASBAHTU A'LAA A'HDIKA WA WA'DIKA MAS TATA'T\nI begin my day keeping my covenant and promise to You as much as I can.\nاَبُوْءُ لَكَ بِالنِّعْمَةِ\nABOO'U LAKA BIN NI'MAH\nI confess of Your favor to me\nوَاَسْتَغْفِرُكَ مِنَ الذُّنُوْبِ الَّتِيْ لَا يَغْفِرُهَا غَيْرُكَ\nWA ASTAGHFIRUKA MINADH DHUNOOBIL LATEE LAA YAGHFIRUHAA GHAYRUK\nand I beseech You to forgive my sins that none else can forgive.\nيَا مَنْ هُوَ فِيْ عُلُوِّهٖ دَانٍ\nYAA MAN HUWA FEE U'LUWWIHEE DAAN\nO He Who is nigh in His sublimity,\nوَفِيْ دُنُوِّهٖ عَالٍ\nWA FEE DUNUWWIHEE A'AL\nSublime in His nearness,\nوَفِيْ اِشْرَاقِهٖ مُنِيْرٌ\nWA FEE ISHRAAQIHEE MUNEER\nBrilliant in His glow,\nوَفِيْ سُلْطَانِهٖ قَوِيٌّ\nWA FEE SULTAANIHEE QAWIYY\nand Powerful in His [absolute] authority!\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِهِ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\n(please) Send blessings upon Muhammad and his Household.",
  "merits": "In his book of Jamal al-Usbu', Sayyid Ibn Tawus has recorded a special prayer and supplication for each of the Holy Imams (a.s.), to be offered on Fridays.\nImam al-Kazim (a.s.)'s prayer consists of two units. In each unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) twelve times."
}
